\name{cellucid_figure_export}
\alias{cellucid_figure_export}
\title{Export the figure}
\usage{
cellucid_figure_export(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{files} (The figures written: one file, or several in one ZIP archive), \code{zip} (The files were written in one ZIP archive (several formats or resolutions)).
}
\description{
Write the figure of the view shown (every view in a grid when the settings say so) as its Download button does, with the figure export's settings as they are (figure_export_set changes them: format, size, labels, legend, style): one SVG or PNG file, or several in one ZIP archive. Refused, saying why, when the figure cannot reproduce what the view shows (a render mode other than points, an overlay it cannot draw).
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{figure.export} (Exports). It acts outside the viewer's state and history (a file the person receives in the browser, a publication, or what the browser keeps for later visits), which Undo does not take back: it makes no step of the history.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (writes-file); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_figure_export(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
